what you drank,
what you played.

3597
02:51:03,294 --> 02:51:05,462
Today, it's like
checking into an airport.

3598
02:51:05,505 --> 02:51:09,132
If you order room service,
you're lucky if you
get it by Thursday.

3599
02:51:10,260 --> 02:51:13,679
Today it's all gone.
A whale shows up
with $4 million in a suitcase

3600
02:51:13,763 --> 02:51:15,847
and some
25-year-old hotel school kid

3601
02:51:15,974 --> 02:51:18,058
is gonna want his
Social Security number.

3602
02:51:20,186 --> 02:51:22,187
After the Teamsters
got knocked out of the box,

3603
02:51:22,272 --> 02:51:25,649
the corporations tore down
practically all
the old casinos.

3604
02:51:26,609 --> 02:51:29,653
And where did
the money come from
to rebuild the pyramids?

3605
02:51:30,446 --> 02:51:31,822
Junk bonds.

3606
02:51:37,412 --> 02:51:38,996
SAM: Still not sure?

3607
02:51:39,539 --> 02:51:41,415
Probable. Maybe questionable.

3608
02:51:41,499 --> 02:51:43,875
Let me know as soon
as you can find out.

3609
02:51:45,503 --> 02:51:48,630
SAM: But in the end,
I wound up right
back where I started.

3610
02:51:48,715 --> 02:51:50,549
I could still pick winners

3611
02:51:50,633 --> 02:51:54,052
and I could still make money
for all kinds of
people back home.

3612
02:51:54,137 --> 02:51:56,138
And why mess up a good thing?

3613
02:51:57,181 --> 02:51:58,765
And that's that.

3614
02:54:33,379 --> 02:54:35,213
(STARDUST PLAYlNG)

3615
02:54:35,256 --> 02:54:38,967
Sometimes I wonder why
I spend the lonely nights

3616
02:54:41,554 --> 02:54:43,597
Dreaming of a song

3617
02:54:45,975 --> 02:54:49,978
The melody haunts my reverie

3618
02:54:53,733 --> 02:54:55,901
And I am once again with you

3619
02:55:00,698 --> 02:55:02,782
When our love was new

3620
02:55:04,410 --> 02:55:07,329
And each kiss an inspiration

3621
02:55:10,208 --> 02:55:12,417
Ah, but that was long ago

3622
02:55:14,420 --> 02:55:16,755
And now my consolation

3623
02:55:16,797 --> 02:55:18,965
Is in the stardust of a song

3624
02:55:23,387 --> 02:55:25,472
Beside a garden wall

3625
02:55:25,973 --> 02:55:27,974
When stars were bright

3626
02:55:28,601 --> 02:55:30,519
And you were in my arms

3627
02:55:33,147 --> 02:55:36,191
The nightingale
told his fairy tale

3628
02:55:41,322 --> 02:55:44,866
Of paradise where roses grew

3629
02:55:50,373 --> 02:55:52,290
Though I dream in vain

3630
02:55:56,629 --> 02:56:00,590
In my heart it will remain

3631
02:56:03,386 --> 02:56:05,470
My stardust melody

3632
02:56:06,847 --> 02:56:11,851
The memory of love's refrain

